prompt-pr.md:7:REVIEW: read the whole diff (gh pr diff N), the PR description, and the docs/ARCHITECTURE.md sections of every file it touches. gh pr checkout N, build and run test.cmd on the PR branch, then switch back to master and leave the tree clean. Sort what you find into three groups:
prompt-pr.md:13:C. Problems only the author can sensibly fix: the change does not do what it claims, it breaks a provider or mode in a way you can't repair without guessing the author's intent, it removes a feature or provider with no replacement and no issue asking for it, it deletes or weakens unit tests or the version/package guards, it doesn't build or its tests fail for reasons you can't fix, or it conflicts with master in a way you can't resolve without guessing. For these, do NOT close the PR: request changes. Comment thanking the author, list each problem concretely (file and behavior, not vague wording) and what would make it mergeable, and leave it open. The watcher reviews the PR again when the author pushes new commits.
prompt-pr.md:19:- Behind master or conflicting: if the PR allows maintainer edits, merge master into the PR branch, resolve the conflicts keeping both sides' intent, build and test, and push to the PR branch. Otherwise, if GitHub can still merge it, go ahead; if not, request changes asking the author to rebase.
prompt-pr.md:23:1. Merge it on GitHub, then pull master locally.
prompt-pr.md:24:2. Fix the group B problems on master in a follow-up commit. Keep the fixes minimal and don't rewrite the author's work in your own style.
prompt-pr.md:27:5. Build Release and run test.cmd. If either fails and you can't fix it with certainty, stop: do not publish. Revert the merge on master (git revert -m 1), push the revert, comment on the PR with the failure and what the author can do, reopen it if GitHub closed it, and report it as failed.
prompt-pr.md:30:8. Reply on the PR thanking the developer: mention the published version and the README credit, and briefly list any follow-up fixes you made on master so they can see what changed. Make sure it is closed.
prompt-issue.md:12:- Clear bug or small, well-defined feature: fix it on master, following CLAUDE.md and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md (read the relevant sections first):
prompt-issue.md:13:  1. Pull master, then make the smallest fix that solves the reported problem. Don't refactor, rename, reformat or "improve" unrelated code, don't change existing defaults, and make new behavior opt-in when existing users might not want it. Add or update unit tests where the code is testable.

